// `internal` in a single-file program with no imports. This was
// test/fail/visibility_internal_unimplemented until Phase 5 landed package scope:
// while the semantics were unimplemented, refusing the word was the only honest
// answer, and now that they are implemented the same source must compile and run.
//
// Kept as a pass test rather than deleted because the flat entry point is its own
// path — there are no module boundaries, so the declaring and the using side are
// both the entry module, and check_module_ref_visibility must take the same-prefix
// early exit without ever consulting package identity. Were that exit missing, a
// flat program's own `internal` name would be refused against itself.
//
// The cross-package refusal is test/fail/visibility_internal_cross_package.sf and
// same-package acceptance is test/pass/visibility_module_ok.sf; this pins the
// degenerate case between them.
internal fun packaged_helper(): Int {
    return 1
}

var result: Int = packaged_helper()
IO.println(result)
